<!DOCTYPE airframe SYSTEM "../airframe.dtd">
<!-- SUPERSEDED by openuas_zohd_talon_250g_optim_002.xml: the PITCH_NEUTRAL_DEFAULT change in this file has no effect with ahrs float_cmpl_quat / ins alt_float; iteration 2 uses COMMAND_PITCH_TRIM instead. Do not fly this file. -->
<airframe name="Talon_250G">
  <description>
   Small foam airframe to test UWB swarm behavior and ETECS control

    + MODEL:            ZoHD Talon 250G
    + FLIGHTCONTROLLER: FlyingRC F4 v1.5 as Mateksys F405-TE-SD
    + IMU:              ICM42688-P
    + ACTUATORS:        JX PDI-1143HB 4.3g
    + GNSS              uBlox M10 GNSS
    + MAGNETOMETER:     QMC5883L on GNSS module, optionally RM3100
    + ESC:              HAKRC 32A 35A
    + RCRX:             OpenR-XSR
    + AIRSPEED:         Sensirion SDP33
    + TELEMETRY:        Mesh 433mHz LoRa or temporary XBEE S1 Pro Digimesh
    + BARO:             Infineon DPS310
    + CURRENT:          FC onboard sensor on the default analog ports
    + RANGEFINDER:      Surertech VB22A on I2C
    + MOTOR:            1406 - 2600Kv Brushless outrunner 12 poles
    + PROPELLER:        Default 2 Blade 5x5in Right
    + BATTERY:          18650 Li-Ion 2S1P INR18650 3300mAh

    NOTES:
    + ServoPins on PCB point to lift side of airframe
    + The FC (FlightController) PCB is mounted with the F4 MCU towards the bottom of the airframe
    + Battery voltage and current via onboard sensor
    + Servos powered via BEC on FC
    + FC powered via BEC on FC
    + Telemetry powered via FC MCU LDO 3v3 pin output
    + GNSS powered via FC 5v pad
    + C3 Module as MCU for UWB only powered via onboard BEC
    + Uploading of the firmware can be performed via USB using the availabe Bootloader
      Also possible via USB DFU-UTIL after pressing the boot button on the FC
    + On an I2C port we have Barometer, Magnetometer, Airspeed and Rangefinder
    + GNSS set to ~17Hz update rate, 4 constelations, SBAS enabled
    + Regular battery for this airframe is a 3300mAh 2S LiIon min. 5C
    + ESC set to fixed endpoints 1100-1900us
    + RC RX powered via FC 5v
    + On the R81 SBUS out channel 9 gives the RSSI value RX output , can be used in FC for OSD
    + Vision: added a JeVois "clone" created from RPI Zero 2W with AI cam on UART1 TX/RX
    + HAKRC 32A 35A with AM32 firmware v2.21 patched to fix kV value bug in v2.20 firmware
  </description>

